# Dropped from the Arch list (reason in parens):
# asdcontrol (Apple Silicon only, N/A on x86_64 Fedora)
# expac (pacman tooling; use dnf repoquery)
# gnome-themes-extra (retired in Fedora)
# lazydocker (no RPM; install upstream binary manually)
# moonlight-qt (no RPM; Flathub com.moonlight_stream.Moonlight)
# obsidian (no RPM; Flathub md.obsidian.Obsidian)
# pacman-contrib (pacman tooling; use dnf clean/autoremove)
# qt6-multimedia, qt6-multimedia-ffmpeg (superseded by OWE; shell is image-only, video via OWE lock feed)
# tzupdate (available as an optional Omadora COPR RPM; Fedora uses chrony)
# ufw, ufw-docker (replaced by firewalld; see install/config/firewall.sh)
# webp-pixbuf-loader (retired; WebP is in gdk-pixbuf2)
# yay (Arch-only AUR helper; dnf + COPR replace it)
# inetutils (split into hostname/telnet/tftp/ftp above)
# bluez-utils (merged into bluez on Fedora)
# qt6-multimedia-ffmpeg (bundled in qt6-qtmultimedia)
